    "date": "2026-08-18",
    "insight": "vLLM's MBT token budget is a load-dependent optimum, not a constant (P-PAS, arXiv:2608.15171, Aug 15 2026). Chunked prefill fixed head-of-line blocking but left the coupling: prefill cost is paid ONCE per request, while iteration wall-clock is paid by EVERY decoding sequence on EVERY token — so a large budget's cost scales with decode population while its benefit doesn't. Large chunks are free at 2 concurrent seqs and ruinous at 40. Ship a policy, not a number.",
